  "gear": "New Balance Hierro v8  Shadow Grey",
  "description": "Nighttime temperatures starting to get into the 20s. Everything covered in frost in the morning but then just absolutely roasted on Snow Mesa. It wasn't actually even that hot, just not a cloud in the sky made it feel like a microwave. I'll take it over being cold and wet every time. Properly back in the mountains now so the views are back! Hitched the very first car into Lake City with Travis from Texas who is in his 60s with quite the peak bagging resume, very impressed. The Lake City hiker center is a godsend, operated by the best people and so useful. Felt some of that trail magic I haven't felt since Hiker Heaven on the PCT. A lady took my clothes to put in the wash across the street. They have bikes to get around town! Checked into a motel on the phone and they told me to just walk in and we'll settle up in the morning. LAKE CITY CITY OF CHAMPIONS. \n\nI will probably zero here tomorrow? I've got 125 miles left so about 5 days, but it's 50 miles to Silverton and we are scheduled for some thunderstorms on Saturday. Everything between here and Silverton is extremely exposed and between 12 and 14k feet. I'm a little scarred right now and I'm not sure the best way to try to execute this. Push all the way to Durango? Zero here? Double zero here to completely wait out the storm? Leave tomorrow and try to be at the storm to zero in Silverton? It 's getting colder every night too though.  For now I will just go eat.",
